  <section xml:id="introduction-what-is">
    <title>What is &productname;?</title>
    <!--xi:include xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" href="snip-product-description.xml"/-->
    <para>
      &productname; is a technology and support solution for mixed Linux environments. With a &productname; subscription, you can update &rhel; from repositories provided by &suse;. This means you get support from &suse; with no requirement to migrate your existing infrastructure to a different operating system.
      It provides continuous security patches, updates and maintenance.
      Customers can migrate to &productname; by simply removing their &rh; channels and installing the &suse; channels. This process does not cause any downtime. The &rh; or &centos; package manager yum/dnf is still used; the only change is the repository location.
      No migration is required, allowing you to maintain your existing infrastructure while benefiting from comprehensive &suse; support.
    </para>
    <!-- Gemini:
     SUSE Multi-Linux Support (SMLS) is a unified technology and support solution designed for mixed Linux environments. By switching repository locations to SUSE-provided channels without downtime, administrators can maintain Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) and CentOS Linux systems with continuous security patches, updates and maintenance. SMLS provides 100% binary compatibility at the application programming interface (API) and application binary interface (ABI) levels, allowing organizations to retain their existing infrastructure and run certified workloads without migrating to a new operating system.
     -->
    <para>
      &productname; is a support offering, not a new Linux distribution. The patches, packages and maintenance provided keep the same Application Binary Interface (ABI), making them identical for applications. As a result, Linux systems maintained by &suse; are fully compatible at the ABI level with supported &rhla; and &centos; versions. Applications that run on &rhla; are expected to have equivalent performance and functionality when run on Linux maintained with &productname;. However, customers are advised to thoroughly test their specific applications before running production workloads.
      &productname; is a 100% binary-compatible version of &rhla; (including API and ABI 100% compatibility). This ensures that applications certified for &rhla; run seamlessly on &reponame; without any modifications.
    </para>
    <para>
      An optional &ha; extension is also available.
    </para>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="introduction-liberty-linux">
    <title>What was &reponame;?</title>
    <para>
      &reponame; was the former name for &suse;'s offering that provided support for environments
      using a 100% binary-compatible version of &rhla;. It has now been integrated into &productname;.
      You may still encounter references to <quote>&reponame;</quote> as part of the &productname;
      service. The underlying software components, such as channels and repositories, are still
      named &reponame;.
    </para>
    <para>
      The name change reflects the service-oriented nature of &productname; and &suse;'s commitment
      to supporting multiple Linux distributions within a unified service, emphasizing its
      capability to handle complex, heterogeneous Linux environments. Additionally, it avoids the
      misunderstanding of perceiving it as another Linux distribution.
    </para>
  </section>

